<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely unchanged.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely unchanged on Wednesday, with only the one and two-month rates lower, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the PHIBOR rates mirrored the soft trends in the overnight money market where rates were steady amid high liquidity.</p>
<p>The Central Bank had kept a floor on rates through its overnight borrowing rate at 10.25 percent.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 12	     MARCH 11</p>
<p>    1 W		9  5/16		 9  5/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  5/16		 9  5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9  5/16		 9  3/8</p>
<p>    2 M		9  1/2		  9  9/16</p>
<p>    3 M		9  5/8		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    6 M		9  7/8		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    12M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		13-Mar		  12-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
